body:
`@objectstack/driver-sql` DTS build was intermittently failing with `TS2306: File '…/spec/dist/system/index.d.ts' is not a module` in CI. The flat `types` condition on spec's subpath exports always directed `moduleResolution: "bundler"` to the CJS declaration file, whose `.js`-suffixed chunk imports (`'../object.zod-BntYUReb.js'`) rely on an indirect `.js` → `.d.ts` lookup that TypeScript 6 resolves non-deterministically under CI load.

## Changes

- **`packages/spec/package.json`** — migrated all 16 subpath exports (including root `.`) from a flat `types` condition to nested `import`/`require` conditions:

```json
// before
"./system": {
  "types": "./dist/system/index.d.ts",
  "import": "./dist/system/index.mjs",
  "require": "./dist/system/index.js"
}

// after
"./system": {
  "import": { "types": "./dist/system/index.d.mts", "default": "./dist/system/index.mjs" },
  "require": { "types": "./dist/system/index.d.ts",  "default": "./dist/system/index.js"  }
}
```

`moduleResolution: "bundler"` now follows the `import` branch and lands on `index.d.mts`, whose `.mjs`-suffixed chunk imports resolve deterministically to `.d.mts` counterparts — no indirect lookup needed. CJS consumers are unaffected; they continue to get `index.d.ts` via the `require` branch.
